  {"id":55719,"slug":"eristalis-tenax","sci":"Eristalis tenax","common":"Common Drone Fly","family":"Syrphidae","obs":5470,"regions":["north-cascades","central-cascades","rainier","south-cascades","gorge","olympics","oregon-cascades"],"months":[5,6,7,8,9,10],"photos":[{"id":19770890,"ext":"jpg","by":"hobiecat","lic":"CC BY-NC"},{"id":16984655,"ext":"jpg","by":"Drepanostoma","lic":"CC BY"},{"id":101116803,"ext":"jpeg","by":"Gianni Del Bufalo bygdb","lic":"CC BY"},{"id":13239991,"ext":"jpg","by":"Ferran Turmo Gort","lic":"CC BY-NC-SA"},{"id":255290989,"ext":"jpg","by":"Philip Mark Osso","lic":"CC BY-NC"}],"wiki":"Eristalis tenax","summary":"Eristalis tenax is a hoverfly, also known as the drone fly (or \"dronefly\"). It is migratory and cosmopolitan, the most widely distributed syrphid species in the world, and is known from all regions except the Antarctic. It has been introduced into North America and is widely established."},
